{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And men struggle and they strike a pregnant woman.</b> They were not aiming at her. <b>And there is no harm,</b> to the woman. <b>As the master of the woman shall lay upon him.</b> And not as other assessments the woman lays upon him, because the woman has no share and claim in the children. For even though Scripture mentions 'her children,' the intention is not that they are hers, but they are a deposit with her, like a man who deposits a deposit in the domain of his fellow — wherever the deposit is, it is in the domain of its master. Therefore he has the right to set the payment as his own, and to have the one who caused harm punished according to his word; and if he were to set a penalty greater than their value, for that reason it says: <b>and he shall give through the judges (בפלילים)</b> — that is, according to what the judges see fit. And so they interpreted in the Mekhilta: 'As the master of the woman shall lay upon him' — might I understand whatever he wants? Scripture says: 'and he shall give through the judges (בפלילים).' And פלילים means none other than judges."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:02:40.698378943Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}